coi mi'e .kribacr.

First, I would like to apologize for having more or less disappeared from
the lojban community. Life happened, and I'm just now able to enjoy more
free time to where I want to get back into the community. My new career is
one of streaming on the internet. It keeps me busy, but I'd like to get
back into lojban, and most specifically teaching it. I'd like to start
streaming lojbanic lessons on twitch.tv (or justin.tv) where it's just me
talking with the audience, fielding questions, using notepad or something
similar as a whiteboard, and running through the language. I'm not sure how
often I would do it, or exactly when, but I have a lot of interest already
drummed up via my normal audience, and was hoping to drum up interest here
for teacher's aides and other people with whom to converse.

I'm posting this to both mailing lists because I'm looking to drum up
experts and novices alike. :) Let me know if anyone's interested in
participating either way.

mu'o mi'e .kribacr.

